Z||000000||BAM-BAM||03-13-2000||09:46 PM||||  I was wondering, do any of you Fiero aficianatos know where a guy could get his hands on a "NEW" wire loom for an 85GT, or is this an ureasonalbe request? Not that I am in need of one at this time, but when I get to that part of my project I want no stone left unturned and no avenue left unexplored <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">. I would like to replace the old one if possible. Also, are there any routing diagrams for the wire loom? Mine is rather tight in spots. <P>  Thanx Y'all<BR>  BAM-BAM <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||03-13-2000||11:28 PM||||Because your car is a notchback, you may be in luck. It would seem that your GT would have the same wiring as any v6 notchback up to the 88's. You might could find more info by comparing the wiring diagrams in one of the repair manuals. Be warned- the wiring harness for a fastback is very different, especially the engine bay/tail lights harness.||||reg||1
